Adopted unmodified (an origin comment was added to each file):
  configs/intellij/Kingsrook_Code_Style.xml           (qqq-dev-tools/intellij/Kingsrook_Code_Style.xml)
  configs/intellij/Kingsrook_Copyright_Profile.xml    (qqq-dev-tools/intellij/Kingsrook_Copyright_Profile.xml)
  configs/intellij/live-templates/Kingsrook-Java.xml  (qqq-dev-tools/intellij/live-templates/Kingsrook-Java.xml)
  configs/intellij/live-templates/Kingsrook-SQL.xml   (qqq-dev-tools/intellij/live-templates/Kingsrook-SQL.xml)
  configs/eclipse/eclipse-formatter.xml               (qctl eclipse-formatter.xml)
  configs/java/checkstyle/kingsrook-checkstyle.xml    (checkstyle/config.xml)

Adopted with modifications (changes are listed at the top of each file):
  configs/java/checkstyle/checkstyle.xml              (derived from checkstyle/config.xml)
  configs/intellij/project/.idea/codeStyles/Project.xml (derived from Kingsrook_Code_Style.xml)

The prose rules in standards/coding/README.md restate the Kingsrook CODE_STYLE.md
(https://github.com/QRun-IO/qqq/blob/develop/CODE_STYLE.md) as KofTwentyTwo
requirements, and extend them to languages other than Java.
